        "original_id": "39a73107-a4fd-5fd1-890f-544976ddf1b9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Micky Dolenz, George Michael Dolenz Jr., Jesse James Dupree, Samantha Juste, Jacki Bond\n- Organizations: the Monkees, Jackyl, BBC, Top of the Pops, Strike, Go\n- Roles: actor, musician, television director, radio personality, theater director, vocalist, drummer, lead singer, guitarist, songwriter, co-host\n\nFacts:\n- George Michael Dolenz Jr. was born on March 8, 1945.\n- Micky Dolenz is the stage name of George Michael Dolenz Jr., an American actor, musician, television director, radio personality, and theater director.\n- Micky Dolenz was best known as a vocalist and drummer of the 1960s pop/rock band the Monkees.\n- In 1968, Samantha Juste married Micky Dolenz of the Monkees.\n- In 1991, Jesse James Dupree founded the rock band Jackyl.\n- Jesse James Dupree is the lead singer, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Jackyl.\n- Samantha Juste co-hosted BBC television's Top of the Pops.\n- Jacki Bond came from South London.\n- Jacki Bond and Samantha Juste were two British female vocalists signed to Strike, with Samantha Juste signed through its subsidiary Go.",
